IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vic-nouns`
IMPORT `vic-interpretation-time`

-- Part II -- Provisions applicable to Acts, ss 14 to 21A.

§ `Part II -- Provisions applicable to Acts (continued)`

§§ `s 14 Provision as to effect of repeal etc. of Acts`

-- s 14(1): an Act or provision that had been repealed by the first-mentioned Act or provision is not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, construed as revived by the repeal, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of the first-mentioned one.
-- src:140 | (1) Where an Act or a provision of an Act—
-- src:141 | (a) is repealed; or
-- src:142 | (b) expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect—
-- src:143 | any Act or provision of an Act that had been repealed by the first-mentioned Act or provision shall not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, be construed as having been revived in consequence of the repeal, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of the first-mentioned Act or provision.
@ref s 14(1) (src:140-143)
GIVEN event IS A VicEndOfOperation, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s14(1) the Act or provision that the ending Act or provision had repealed is construed as revived` MEANS
    IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE VicThingTheEndingOfAnActMightAffect IS ONE OF
    VicAnythingNotInForceOrExistingAtThatTime              -- (c)
    VicThePreviousOperationOrAnythingDulyDoneOrSuffered    -- (d)
    VicARightPrivilegeObligationOrLiabilityAcquiredAccruedOrIncurred   -- (e)
    VicAnImmunityOrIndemnityConferredOrGiven               -- (ea)
    VicAPenaltyForfeitureOrPunishmentIncurredForAnOffence  -- (f)
    VicAnythingElse

-- s 14(2)(c) to (f): the repeal, amendment, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect does not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, revive or affect the thing.
-- src:144 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act—
-- src:145 | (a) is repealed or amended; or
-- src:146 | (b) expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect—
-- src:147 | the repeal, amendment, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of that Act or provision shall not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears—
-- src:148 | (c) revive anything not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal, amendment, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect becomes operative;
-- src:149 | (d) affect the previous operation of that Act or provision or anything duly done or suffered under that Act or provision;
-- src:150 | (e) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under that Act or provision;
-- src:152 | (ea) affect any immunity or indemnity conferred or given by or under that Act or provision;
-- src:153 | (f) affect any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against that Act or provision; or
-- src:155 | (g) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of anything mentioned in paragraphs (e) to (f)—
-- src:156 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed, as if that Act or provision had not been repealed or amended or had not expired, lapsed or otherwise ceased to have effect.
@ref s 14(2) (src:144-156)
GIVEN thing IS A VicThingTheEndingOfAnActMightAffect, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s14(2)(c)-(f) the repeal, amendment, expiry or lapsing revives or affects the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN VicAnythingElse THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 14(2)(g): it does not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, affect an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of anything mentioned in paragraphs (e) to (f); the text lists (e), (ea) and (f) between those two paragraphs and the encoding counts all three.
-- src:155 | (g) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of anything mentioned in paragraphs (e) to (f)—
@ref s 14(2)(g) (src:155)
GIVEN inRespectOfARightLiabilityImmunityOrPenalty IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s14(2)(g) the repeal, amendment, expiry or lapsing affects an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT inRespectOfARightLiabilityImmunityOrPenalty THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 14(2), closing words: any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed, as if the Act or provision had not been repealed, amended, expired, lapsed or ceased to have effect.
-- src:144 | (2) Where an Act or a provision of an Act—
-- src:145 | (a) is repealed or amended; or
-- src:146 | (b) expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect—
-- src:147 | the repeal, amendment, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of that Act or provision shall not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears—
-- src:148 | (c) revive anything not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal, amendment, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect becomes operative;
-- src:149 | (d) affect the previous operation of that Act or provision or anything duly done or suffered under that Act or provision;
-- src:150 | (e) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under that Act or provision;
-- src:152 | (ea) affect any immunity or indemnity conferred or given by or under that Act or provision;
-- src:153 | (f) affect any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence committed against that Act or provision; or
-- src:155 | (g) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of anything mentioned in paragraphs (e) to (f)—
-- src:156 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed, as if that Act or provision had not been repealed or amended or had not expired, lapsed or otherwise ceased to have effect.
@ref s 14(2) (src:144-156)
GIVEN inRespectOfARightLiabilityImmunityOrPenalty IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s14(2) the proceeding may be instituted, continued or enforced, or the penalty imposed, as if the Act had not been repealed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT inRespectOfARightLiabilityImmunityOrPenalty THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 14(2A): without limiting subsection (2), the repeal, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of such a provision does not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, affect the operation of the savings or transitional provision, end its effect of making a thing effective, or affect the construction of the reference.
-- src:158 | (2A) Without limiting subsection (2), if a provision of an Act that is of a savings or transitional nature (whether or not the Act describes it as such) or that validates anything that is or may otherwise be invalid or that requires a reference in an Act or subordinate instrument or other instrument or document to, or that relates to, an entity or a class of entity to be construed as a reference to another entity or class of entity—
-- src:159 | (a) is repealed; or
-- src:160 | (b) expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect—
-- src:161 | the repeal, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of that provision does not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, affect the operation of the savings or transitional provision or end the validating effect of the provision or affect the construction of that reference, as the case requires.
@ref s 14(2A) (src:158-161)
GIVEN kindOfProvision IS A VicProvisionProtectedOnRepeal, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s14(2A) the repeal, expiry or lapsing of the provision ends the effect it had` MEANS
    CONSIDER kindOfProvision
    WHEN VicAnyOtherProvision THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 14(3): references in subsections (1), (2) and (2A) to the repeal of an Act or provision include a repeal by implication and a repeal by abrogating or limiting its effect or excluding its application.
-- src:163 | (3) References in subsections (1), (2) and (2A) to the repeal of an Act or of a provision of an Act shall be construed as including references to—
-- src:164 | (a) a repeal effected by implication; and
-- src:165 | (b) a repeal effected by abrogating or limiting the effect of the Act or provision or excluding the application of the Act or provision to any person, subject-matter or circumstance.
@ref s 14(3) (src:163-165)
GIVEN how IS A VicHowRepealed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s14(3) the way of repealing is within the references to repeal in s 14(1), (2) and (2A)` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN VicRepealedExpressly THEN NOTHING
    WHEN VicRepealedByImplication THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicRepealedByAbrogatingOrLimitingItsEffect THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicRepealedByExcludingItsApplication THEN JUST TRUE

§§ `s 15 Effect of repeal etc. of amending Act`

-- s 15(1): the repeal, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of an Act or provision that directly amended another Act or a subordinate instrument (by insertion or substitution of words) does not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, affect the direct amendments or their operation or effect.
-- src:168 | (1) Where an Act or a provision of an Act, being an Act or provision that directly amended another Act or a subordinate instrument (whether by the insertion of words or expressions in that Act or subordinate instrument or the substitution of other words or expressions for words or expressions in that Act or subordinate instrument)—
-- src:169 | (a) is repealed; or
-- src:170 | (b) expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect—
-- src:171 | the repeal, expiry, lapsing or ceasing to have effect of that Act or provision shall not, unless the contrary intention expressly appears, affect in any way the direct amendments made in the other Act or in the subordinate instrument or the operation or effect of those amendments.
@ref s 15(1) (src:168-171)
GIVEN directlyAmendedByInsertionOrSubstitutionOfWords IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s15(1) the ending of the amending Act or provision affects the direct amendments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT directlyAmendedByInsertionOrSubstitutionOfWords THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 15(2): subsection (1) applies to a direct amendment made to a provision of an Act by another provision of that Act as it applies to an amendment of an Act by another Act.
-- src:172 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to a direct amendment made to a provision of an Act by another provision of that Act in the same manner as it applies to a direct amendment made to an Act by another Act.
@ref s 15(2) (src:172)
GIVEN amendedByAnotherProvisionOfTheSameAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s15(2) s 15(1) applies to the amendment` MEANS
    IF amendedByAnotherProvisionOfTheSameAct THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 16 Repeal and re-enactment`

-- s 16(a): where an Act or provision is repealed and re-enacted (with or without modification), unless the contrary intention expressly appears, a reference to the repealed Act or provision is construed as a reference to the re-enacted one.
-- src:176 | (a) any reference in any Act or subordinate instrument to the repealed Act or provision shall be construed as a reference to the re-enacted Act or provision; and
@ref s 16(a) (src:176)
GIVEN repealedAndReEnacted IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s16(a) a reference to the repealed Act or provision is construed as a reference to the re-enacted Act or provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT repealedAndReEnacted THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 16(b): insofar as a subordinate instrument made or other thing done under the repealed Act or provision could have been made or done under the re-enacted one, it has effect as if made or done under the re-enacted one.
-- src:177 | (b) insofar as any subordinate instrument made or other thing done under the repealed Act or provision, or having effect as if so made or done, could have been made or done under the re-enacted Act or provision, it shall have effect as if made or done under the re-enacted Act or provision.
@ref s 16(b) (src:177)
GIVEN repealedAndReEnacted IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears IS A BOOLEAN, couldHaveBeenMadeOrDoneUnderTheReEnactedProvision IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s16(b) the instrument made or thing done has effect as if made or done under the re-enacted Act or provision` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT repealedAndReEnacted THEN JUST FALSE
        IF contraryIntentionExpresslyAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF couldHaveBeenMadeOrDoneUnderTheReEnactedProvision THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 17 Construction of references in Acts to other enactments`

-- s 17(1): a reference in an Act to an Act, a provision, or a subordinate instrument is, unless the contrary intention appears, construed according to what has become of it.
-- src:181 | (1) A reference in an Act to that Act or to any provision of that Act or to any other Act or to any provision of any other Act or to any subordinate instrument or provision of a subordinate instrument shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed—
-- src:182 | (a) if the Act, subordinate instrument or provision in question has been amended, as a reference to the Act, subordinate instrument or provision as amended and in force for the time being;
-- src:183 | (b) if the Act, subordinate instrument or provision in question has been re-enacted or re-made (with or without modification), as a reference to the Act, subordinate instrument or provision as re-enacted or re-made and in force for the time being;
-- src:184 | (c) if the Act, subordinate instrument or provision in question has been re-enacted or re-made (with or without modification) and subsequently amended, as a reference to the Act, subordinate instrument or provision as re-enacted or re-made and as subsequently amended and in force for the time being; and
-- src:185 | (d) if the Act, subordinate instrument or provision in question has been repealed and not re-enacted or re-made, as a reference to the Act, subordinate instrument or provision as in force immediately before its repeal.
@ref s 17(1) (src:181-185)
GIVEN state IS A VicStateOfEnactmentReferredTo, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicReadsAs
`s17(1) a reference in an Act to another enactment is construed as a reference to` MEANS
    IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER state
         WHEN VicStillAsFirstMade THEN NOTHING
         WHEN VicHasBeenAmended THEN JUST VicTheEnactmentAsAmendedAndInForceForTheTimeBeing
         WHEN VicHasBeenReEnactedOrReMade THEN JUST VicTheEnactmentAsReEnactedOrReMadeAndInForceForTheTimeBeing
         WHEN VicHasBeenReEnactedOrReMadeAndSubsequentlyAmended THEN JUST VicTheEnactmentAsReEnactedOrReMadeAndSubsequentlyAmendedAndInForceForTheTimeBeing
         WHEN VicHasBeenRepealedAndNotReEnactedOrReMade THEN JUST VicTheEnactmentAsInForceImmediatelyBeforeItsRepeal

-- s 17(1A): a reference in an Act to a provision of an Act or subordinate instrument that has been renumbered or relocated is construed as a reference to the provision as renumbered or relocated and in force for the time being, unless the contrary intention appears.
-- src:187 | (1A) A reference in an Act to any provision of that or any other Act or to any provision of a subordinate instrument must, if the provision in question has been renumbered or relocated, be construed as a reference to the provision as renumbered or relocated and in force for the time being, unless the contrary intention appears.
@ref s 17(1A) (src:187)
GIVEN referenceIsToAProvision IS A BOOLEAN, provisionRenumberedOrRelocated IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicReadsAs
`s17(1A) a reference in an Act to a provision that has been renumbered or relocated is construed as a reference to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT referenceIsToAProvision THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT provisionRenumberedOrRelocated THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST VicTheProvisionAsRenumberedOrRelocatedAndInForceForTheTimeBeing

DECLARE VicLegislationOfAnotherPlace IS ONE OF
    VicACommonwealthAct
    VicAnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrOfATerritory
    VicAnInstrumentOfALegislativeCharacterMadeUnderACommonwealthAct
    VicAnInstrumentOfALegislativeCharacterMadeUnderAnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrOfATerritory
    VicAnythingElse2

-- s 17(2)(a): in s 17, a reference to an Act includes a Commonwealth Act and an Act or Ordinance of another State or of a Territory.
-- src:190 | (a) a reference to an Act includes a reference to—
-- src:191 | (i) a Commonwealth Act; and
-- src:192 | (ii) an Act or Ordinance of another State or of a Territory;
@ref s 17(2)(a) (src:190-192)
GIVEN thing IS A VicLegislationOfAnotherPlace
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s17(2)(a) a reference to an Act in s 17 includes` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN VicACommonwealthAct THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicAnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrOfATerritory THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 17(2)(b): in s 17, a reference to a subordinate instrument includes an instrument of a legislative character made or to be made under a Commonwealth Act and under an Act or Ordinance of another State or of a Territory.
-- src:193 | (b) a reference to a subordinate instrument includes a reference to an instrument of a legislative character made or to be made under or pursuant to the provisions of—
-- src:194 | (i) a Commonwealth Act; and
-- src:195 | (ii) an Act or Ordinance of another State or of a Territory.
@ref s 17(2)(b) (src:193-195)
GIVEN thing IS A VicLegislationOfAnotherPlace
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s17(2)(b) a reference to a subordinate instrument in s 17 includes` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN VicAnInstrumentOfALegislativeCharacterMadeUnderACommonwealthAct THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN VicAnInstrumentOfALegislativeCharacterMadeUnderAnActOrOrdinanceOfAnotherStateOrOfATerritory THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 18 References in Acts to provisions of subordinate instruments`

-- s 18: a reference in an Act to a regulation, rule, by-law, local law, proclamation, Order in Council, order, scheme or other provision is, unless the context otherwise requires, a reference to one contained in a subordinate instrument made under the Act in which the reference occurs.
-- src:198 | 18 References in Acts to provisions of subordinate instruments
-- src:199 | Where in an Act reference is made to a regulation, rule, by-law, local law, proclamation, Order in Council, order, scheme or other provision, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as a reference to a regulation, rule, by-law, local law, proclamation, Order in Council, order, scheme or other provision (as the case requires) contained in a subordinate instrument made or to be made under or pursuant to the provisions of the Act in which the reference occurs.
@ref s 18 (src:198-199)
GIVEN containedInASubordinateInstrumentMadeOrToBeMadeUnderThatAct IS A BOOLEAN, contextOtherwiseRequires IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s18 the reference is construed as a reference to one contained in a subordinate instrument made under that Act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF contextOtherwiseRequires THEN JUST FALSE
        IF containedInASubordinateInstrumentMadeOrToBeMadeUnderThatAct THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 19 Citation of references in Acts`

DECLARE VicUnitCitedByNumber IS ONE OF
    VicChapter
    VicPart
    VicSectionOrSchedule
    VicScheduleNotCitedByNumber
    VicDivision
    VicSubdivision
    VicSubsection
    VicParagraphOfASectionSubsectionInterpretationOrSchedule
    VicParagraphOfAClauseSubclauseItemColumnTableOrFormInASchedule
    VicSubparagraph
    VicSubSubparagraph
    VicTableOfASectionOrSubsection
    VicClauseItemColumnTableOrFormOfASchedule
    VicSubclause
    VicSubSubclause

DECLARE VicWhereTheCitedUnitIs IS ONE OF
    VicInTheChapterOfTheActInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInThePartOfTheChapterInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInThePartOfTheActInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheSectionOrScheduleOfOrToTheActInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheOnlyScheduleToTheActInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheDivisionOfThePartInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheSubdivisionOfTheDivisionInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheSubsectionOfTheSectionInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheParagraphOfTheSectionSubsectionInterpretationOrScheduleInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheParagraphOfTheClauseSubclauseItemColumnTableOrFormOfOrInTheScheduleInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheSubparagraphOfTheParagraphInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheSubSubparagraphOfTheSubparagraphInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheTableOfOrInTheSectionOrSubsectionInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheClauseItemColumnTableOrFormOfOrInTheScheduleInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheSubclauseOfTheClauseInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
    VicInTheSubSubclauseOfTheSubclauseInWhichTheReferenceOccurs

-- s 19(1): where a provision of an Act refers to a unit by a number, the reference is, unless the context otherwise requires, construed as a reference to the unit so designated in the place the paragraph names.
-- src:202 | (1) Where a provision of an Act refers—
-- src:204 | (aaa) to a Chapter by a number, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as a reference to the Chapter, designated by that number, of the Act in which the reference occurs;
-- src:206 | (aa) to a Part by a number, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed—
-- src:208 | (i) if the Act contains Chapters and the Part number is not a decimal number—as a reference to the Part, designated by that number, of the Chapter in which the reference occurs; or
-- src:210 | (ia) if the Act contains Chapters and the Part number is a decimal number—as a reference to the Part, designated by that number, of the Act in which the reference occurs; or
-- src:211 | (ii) if the Act does not contain Chapters, as a reference to the Part, designated by that number, of the Act in which the reference occurs;
-- src:213 | (a) to a section or Schedule by a number, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as a reference to the section or Schedule, designated by that number, of or to the Act in which the reference occurs;
-- src:214 | (b) to a Schedule but does not refer to it by a number, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, if there is only one Schedule to the Act in which the reference occurs, be construed as a reference to the Schedule to the Act in which the reference occurs; or
-- src:215 | (c) to a Division, Subdivision, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, sub-subparagraph, clause, subclause, sub-subclause, item, column, table or form by a number, the reference shall, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as a reference—
-- src:216 | (i) to the Division, designated by that number, of the Part in which the reference occurs;
-- src:217 | (ii) to the Subdivision, designated by that number, of the Division in which the reference occurs;
-- src:218 | (iii) to the subsection, designated by that number, of the section in which the reference occurs;
-- src:219 | (iv) to the paragraph, designated by that number, of the section, subsection, interpretation or Schedule in which the reference occurs;
-- src:220 | (v) to the paragraph, designated by that number, of the clause, subclause, item, column, table or form of or in the Schedule in which the reference occurs;
-- src:221 | (vi) to the subparagraph, designated by that number, of the paragraph in which the reference occurs;
-- src:222 | (vii) to the sub-subparagraph, designated by that number, of the subparagraph in which the reference occurs;
-- src:223 | (viii) to the table, designated by that number, of or in the section or subsection in which the reference occurs;
-- src:224 | (ix) to the clause, item, column, table or form, designated by that number, of or in the Schedule in which the reference occurs;
-- src:225 | (x) to the subclause, designated by that number, of the clause in which the reference occurs; or
-- src:226 | (xi) to the sub-subclause, designated by that number, of the subclause in which the reference occurs—
-- src:227 | as the case requires.
@ref s 19(1) (src:202-227)
GIVEN unit IS A VicUnitCitedByNumber, actContainsChapters IS A BOOLEAN, partNumberIsADecimalNumber IS A BOOLEAN, scheduleIsTheOnlyOne IS A BOOLEAN, contextOtherwiseRequires IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE VicWhereTheCitedUnitIs
`s19(1) a reference to a unit by number is construed as a reference to the unit` MEANS
    IF contextOtherwiseRequires THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER unit
         WHEN VicChapter THEN JUST VicInTheChapterOfTheActInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicPart THEN
             BRANCH
                 IF actContainsChapters AND NOT partNumberIsADecimalNumber THEN JUST VicInThePartOfTheChapterInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
                 IF actContainsChapters AND partNumberIsADecimalNumber THEN JUST VicInThePartOfTheActInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
                 OTHERWISE JUST VicInThePartOfTheActInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicSectionOrSchedule THEN JUST VicInTheSectionOrScheduleOfOrToTheActInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicScheduleNotCitedByNumber THEN IF scheduleIsTheOnlyOne THEN JUST VicInTheOnlyScheduleToTheActInWhichTheReferenceOccurs ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN VicDivision THEN JUST VicInTheDivisionOfThePartInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicSubdivision THEN JUST VicInTheSubdivisionOfTheDivisionInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicSubsection THEN JUST VicInTheSubsectionOfTheSectionInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicParagraphOfASectionSubsectionInterpretationOrSchedule THEN JUST VicInTheParagraphOfTheSectionSubsectionInterpretationOrScheduleInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicParagraphOfAClauseSubclauseItemColumnTableOrFormInASchedule THEN JUST VicInTheParagraphOfTheClauseSubclauseItemColumnTableOrFormOfOrInTheScheduleInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicSubparagraph THEN JUST VicInTheSubparagraphOfTheParagraphInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicSubSubparagraph THEN JUST VicInTheSubSubparagraphOfTheSubparagraphInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicTableOfASectionOrSubsection THEN JUST VicInTheTableOfOrInTheSectionOrSubsectionInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicClauseItemColumnTableOrFormOfASchedule THEN JUST VicInTheClauseItemColumnTableOrFormOfOrInTheScheduleInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicSubclause THEN JUST VicInTheSubclauseOfTheClauseInWhichTheReferenceOccurs
         WHEN VicSubSubclause THEN JUST VicInTheSubSubclauseOfTheSubclauseInWhichTheReferenceOccurs

DECLARE VicHowAUnitIsDesignated IS ONE OF
    VicANumberExpressedInWordsOrFigures
    VicALetter
    VicACombinationOfANumberSoExpressedAndALetter
    VicSomethingElseAsADesignation

-- s 19(2): in subsection (1) number means a number expressed in words or figures, a letter, or a combination of such a number and a letter.
-- src:228 | (2) In subsection (1) number means—
-- src:229 | (a) a number expressed in words or figures;
-- src:230 | (b) a letter; or
-- src:231 | (c) a combination of a number so expressed and a letter.
@ref s 19(2) (src:228-231)
GIVEN designation IS A VicHowAUnitIsDesignated
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s19(2) the designation is a number for s 19(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER designation
    WHEN VicSomethingElseAsADesignation THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 20 Construction of references in Acts to portions of Acts or subordinate instruments`

-- s 20: a description or citation of a portion of an Act or subordinate instrument is, unless the contrary intention appears, construed as including the word, section, subsection, paragraph, ... mentioned as forming the beginning and as forming the end of the portion.
-- Positions are the ordinal places of the divisions in the enactment; the portion runs from the first to the last, ends included.
-- src:234 | 20 Construction of references in Acts to portions of Acts or subordinate instruments
-- src:235 | In an Act, a description or citation of a portion of that Act or of any other Act or of any subordinate instrument made under that Act or any other Act shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as including the word, section, subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, regulation, rule, by-law, local law, subregulation, subrule, clause, Chapter, Part, Schedule or other division mentioned or referred to as forming the beginning and as forming the end of the portion comprised in the description or citation.
@ref s 20 (src:234-235)
GIVEN firstPosition IS A NUMBER, lastPosition IS A NUMBER, position IS A NUMBER, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s20 the division at a position is within the portion cited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF position AT LEAST firstPosition AND position AT MOST lastPosition THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 21 Meaning of certain expressions in Acts`

DECLARE VicOldReference IS ONE OF
    VicTheColonyOrTheTerritoryOrDistrictOfPortPhillip
    VicTheGovernorOfTheColonyOfNewSouthWales
    VicTheColonialSecretaryOrSuperintendentOfPortPhillip
    VicTheSupremeCourtOrAnotherCourtOfTheColonyOrItsJudgeJusticeOrPresidingPerson
    VicAJusticeOfThePeaceOfTheColony
    VicAnOfficerOrPersonInThePublicServiceOfTheColony
    VicTheGovernmentGazetteOfTheColony

-- s 21(1)(a)-(g): unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in an Imperial Act or an Act of the Governor and Legislative Council of the colony of New South Wales in force in Victoria on 1 July 1851 is construed as stated.
-- src:238 | (1) Unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in an Imperial Act or an Act of the Governor and Legislative Council of the colony of New South Wales in force in Victoria on 1 July 1851—
-- src:239 | (a) to the colony or the colony of New South Wales or the territory of New South Wales or the district of Port Phillip shall be construed as a reference to Victoria;
-- src:240 | (b) to the Governor of the colony of New South Wales shall be construed as a reference to the Governor of Victoria;
-- src:241 | (c) to the Colonial Secretary of the colony of New South Wales or the Superintendent of Port Phillip shall be construed as a reference to the responsible Minister of the Crown in Victoria for the time being administering the provision in which the reference occurs;
-- src:242 | (d) to the Supreme Court of the colony of New South Wales or any judge of that Court or to any other court in that colony or to any judge, justice or other person presiding in any such court shall be construed as a reference to the court, judge or other person having a similar jurisdiction in Victoria;
-- src:243 | (e) to a justice of the peace in and for the colony of New South Wales shall be construed as a reference to a justice of the peace in and for Victoria;
-- src:244 | (f) to any officer or other person in the public service of the colony of New South Wales shall be construed as a reference to an officer or other person having similar duties in the public service of Victoria; and
-- src:245 | (g) to the Government Gazette of the colony of New South Wales shall be construed as a reference to the Victoria Government Gazette.
@ref s 21(1) (src:238-245)
GIVEN old IS A VicOldReference, isAnImperialOrNewSouthWalesActInForceInVictoriaOn1July1851 IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s21(1) a reference in an old Act is construed as a reference to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT isAnImperialOrNewSouthWalesActInForceInVictoriaOn1July1851 THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER old
            WHEN VicTheColonyOrTheTerritoryOrDistrictOfPortPhillip THEN JUST "Victoria"
            WHEN VicTheGovernorOfTheColonyOfNewSouthWales THEN JUST "the Governor of Victoria"
            WHEN VicTheColonialSecretaryOrSuperintendentOfPortPhillip THEN JUST "the responsible Minister of the Crown in Victoria for the time being administering the provision in which the reference occurs"
            WHEN VicTheSupremeCourtOrAnotherCourtOfTheColonyOrItsJudgeJusticeOrPresidingPerson THEN JUST "the court, judge or other person having a similar jurisdiction in Victoria"
            WHEN VicAJusticeOfThePeaceOfTheColony THEN JUST "a justice of the peace in and for Victoria"
            WHEN VicAnOfficerOrPersonInThePublicServiceOfTheColony THEN JUST "an officer or other person having similar duties in the public service of Victoria"
            WHEN VicTheGovernmentGazetteOfTheColony THEN JUST "the Victoria Government Gazette"

-- s 21(2): unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in any Act in force in Victoria on 21 November 1856 to the Legislative Council is a reference to the Legislative Council of Victoria and the Legislative Assembly of Victoria.
-- src:246 | (2) Unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in any Act (by whatsoever Parliament passed) in force in Victoria on 21 November 1856 to the Legislative Council shall be construed as a reference to the Legislative Council of Victoria and the Legislative Assembly of Victoria.
@ref s 21(2) (src:246)
GIVEN actInForceInVictoriaOn21November1856 IS A BOOLEAN, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s21(2) a reference to the Legislative Council in an old Act is construed as a reference to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT actInForceInVictoriaOn21November1856 THEN NOTHING
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST "the Legislative Council of Victoria and the Legislative Assembly of Victoria"

DECLARE VicServiceReferredTo IS ONE OF
    VicNavyOrArmyOrNavalOrMilitaryForcesOrNavalOrMilitaryService
    VicAirForcesOrServiceWithThem
    VicOtherForce

-- s 21(3): unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in any Act to His Majesty's navy or army, naval or military forces, or the naval or military forces of the Commonwealth, or naval or military service, includes a reference to the air forces or service with them.
-- src:248 | (3) Unless the contrary intention appears, a reference in any Act to His Majesty's navy or army or to His Majesty's naval or military forces or to the naval or military forces of the Commonwealth or to naval or military service therewith shall be construed as including a reference to His Majesty's air forces or the air forces of the Commonwealth or to service therewith, as the case requires.
@ref s 21(3) (src:248)
GIVEN service IS A VicServiceReferredTo, contraryIntentionAppears IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s21(3) a reference to naval or military forces or service includes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF contraryIntentionAppears THEN JUST FALSE
        IF service EQUALS VicAirForcesOrServiceWithThem THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `s 21A Incorporation of amendments`

-- s 21A(1): if an Act has been amended, in any reprinting the Government Printer must, unless the Chief Parliamentary Counsel otherwise approves, reprint it as amended.
-- src:252 | (1) If an Act has been amended then in any reprinting of the Act the Government Printer must, unless the Chief Parliamentary Counsel otherwise approves, reprint the Act as so amended.
@ref s 21A(1) (src:252)
GIVEN actHasBeenAmended IS A BOOLEAN, chiefParliamentaryCounselOtherwiseApproves IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s21A(1) the reprint of the Act is as amended` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT actHasBeenAmended THEN JUST FALSE
        IF chiefParliamentaryCounselOtherwiseApproves THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 21A(2): there must be printed in a reprint a reference to each Act or subordinate instrument by which the reprinted Act is amended, and a reference to each amended provision and the amending provision.
-- src:253 | (2) There must be printed in a reprint of an Act—
-- src:254 | (a) a reference to each Act or subordinate instrument by which the reprinted Act is amended; and
-- src:255 | (b) a reference (whether in a sidenote, footnote or endnote) to each provision of the reprinted Act that is amended and the provision of the Act or subordinate instrument by which the amendment is made.
@ref s 21A(2) (src:253-255)
GIVEN isAReprintOfAnAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s21A(2) the reprint must show the amending Acts and instruments and the amended provisions` MEANS
    IF isAReprintOfAnAct THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 21A(3): in reprinting an Act the Government Printer may omit the indorsement on the Act of the date of its passing.
-- src:257 | (3) In reprinting an Act the Government Printer may omit the indorsement on the Act of the date of its passing.
@ref s 21A(3) (src:257)
GIVEN isAReprintOfAnAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s21A(3) the reprint may omit the indorsement of the date of passing` MEANS
    IF isAReprintOfAnAct THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 21A(4): nothing in subsection (3) affects the status of the indorsement as part of the Act.
-- src:259 | (4) Nothing in subsection (3) affects the status of the indorsement as part of the Act.
@ref s 21A(4) (src:259)
GIVEN indorsementOmittedFromAReprint IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s21A(4) omitting the indorsement in a reprint affects its status as part of the Act` MEANS
    IF indorsementOmittedFromAReprint THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
